  "_doc": [
    "The ONLY backtest per-leg MFE distribution that exists in this repo, on the",
    "percent-of-entry basis. It is transcribed from MI-151's published table",
    "(docs/research/ml2-predictive-bracket-2026-09-06.md \u00a7 'The per-leg MFE",
    "distribution'), which is the artifact of trainer run 34041656868 reported in",
    "issue #11154.",
    "",
    "WHY A TRANSCRIPTION AND NOT THE CORPUS: the 9,814-row corpus was produced on",
    "the trainer VM and was never committed. A key census over every committed",
    "corpus in docs/research/ (e35-bracket-corpus.jsonl n=8,520;",
    "e35-bracket-corpus-history.jsonl n=10,547; m20-sweep-corpus.jsonl n=1,379 --",
    "20,446 rows total) finds ZERO keys containing 'mfe', 'peak' or 'excurs',",
    "against a positive control that does return those files' common keys. So the",
    "quantiles below are the whole of the backtest side that a session can reach",
    "without a trainer dispatch.",
    "",
    "THE FIELD THAT MATTERS MOST HERE IS `timeframe`. Every row is 15m. No live",
    "leg runs trend_donchian at 15m (config/strategies.yaml: 1h and 4h only), so",
    "these rows have NO timeframe-matched live counterpart. The consumer",
    "(scripts/research/exit_location_fidelity.py) refuses to join across",
    "timeframe rather than reporting a ratio that is a horizon difference wearing",
    "a fidelity label."
